                        "sense_id": "bc9643c1-37a1-3433-bf62-4dc94066a408",
                        "entry_id": "51682b13-4941-35e3-b47d-26133392e2f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any cruciferous plant of the genus Lepidium, often called garden cresses or pepperworts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "34cbe4e8-991f-49b9-9c01-75d999bdcf59",
                                "sense_id": "bc9643c1-37a1-3433-bf62-4dc94066a408",
                                "text": "Danziger’s new Green Dragon, a delicate and airy Lepidium, is a unique green filler for flower arrangements that blends harmoniously in any centerpiece or bouquet. Green Dragon has a heavier stem than other lepidiums, which won’t tangle with each other, ultimately decreasing breakage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc57074a-708a-496f-9eac-7eec44a5ac37",
                                "sense_id": "bc9643c1-37a1-3433-bf62-4dc94066a408",
                                "text": "There are about 175 different Lepidiums, no doubt some native to your area and some imported."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2098efd-cc3e-4a3e-b209-7e2a1314f799",
                                "sense_id": "bc9643c1-37a1-3433-bf62-4dc94066a408",
                                "text": "Many of the native lepidiums are rare or restricted in distribution, and some have become extinct. […] Aborigines in South Australia steamed bundles of lepidium leaves in earthen pits."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
